<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i-1)) == null) || this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i-1)));</code>

However, the above assert statement seems to incorrectly interpret the requirement. The correct interpretation should be that each element from the index to the old size minus one is shifted to the right by one position, and the new element is placed at the specified index. Here's the corrected version:

<code>assert index >= 0 && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i+1).equals(\old(this.get(i)));</code>

